{
  "originalRequest": "Synthetic teaching example, not a research result. Draw exactly Start → Receive sample → Quality check (diamond). Label yes branch → Normalize → Output → End. Label no branch → Reject sample → End. Use English text. Distinguish operations from decisions and start/end. No numeric or scientific claims. Reference image is for design structure only; do not transfer its paper data or conclusions.",
  "methodology": "Synthetic teaching example, not a research result. Draw exactly Start → Receive sample → Quality check (diamond). Label yes branch → Normalize → Output → End. Label no branch → Reject sample → End. Use English text. Distinguish operations from decisions and start/end. No numeric or scientific claims. Reference image is for design structure only; do not transfer its paper data or conclusions.",
  "visualIntent": "Synthetic sample process",
  "completePlan": "Based on the methodology provided and the visual style of the reference image, here is a detailed description for the illustrative figure.\n\n**Figure Description:**\n\n**Overall Layout and Style:**\nThe figure is a vertical flowchart set against a pure white background. It adopts the visual language of the reference image: flat vector graphics, a specific teal/green color palette, and clean sans-serif typography. The flow moves strictly from top to bottom, branching into two parallel paths in the middle before converging at the bottom.\n\n**Color Palette:**\n*   **Primary Fill (Operations/Start/End):** Teal green (approximate hex #1E8C84), matching the reference blocks.\n*   **Secondary Fill (Decision):** White with a thick teal border.\n*   **Text & Icons:** Pure white inside colored shapes; Teal inside white shapes.\n*   **Connectors:** Solid teal arrows.\n\n**Detailed Elements (Top to Bottom):**\n\n1.  **Start Node:**\n    *   **Shape:** A pill-shaped rectangle (rounded ends).\n    *   **Content:** Filled with solid teal. Contains a white \"Play\" triangle icon (pointing right) on the left and the text **\"Start\"** in white, bold, sans-serif font centered vertically.\n    *   **Connection:** A straight teal arrow points downward to the next block.\n\n2.  **Operation Block 1:**\n    *   **Shape:** A rectangle with slightly rounded corners (similar aspect ratio to reference blocks).\n    *   **Content:** Filled with solid teal. Contains a white icon representing a document or sample (a rectangle with horizontal lines) on the left. The text **\"Receive sample\"** appears to the right of the icon in white.\n    *   **Connection:** A straight teal arrow points downward to the decision diamond.\n\n3.  **Decision Node (Quality Check):**\n    *   **Shape:** A diamond (rhombus).\n    *   **Content:** White fill with a thick teal outline (approx. 3-4px stroke). Inside, there is a teal magnifying glass icon (symbolizing inspection) above the text **\"Quality check\"** written in teal.\n    *   **Connections:** Two arrows emerge from this node:\n        *   **Left Branch (Yes):** An arrow exits the left corner, curves downward, and points to the \"Normalize\" block. This path is labeled with a small teal text box or floating text saying **\"Yes\"**.\n        *   **Right Branch (No):** An arrow exits the right corner, curves downward, and points to the \"Reject sample\" block. This path is labeled with a small teal text box or floating text saying **\"No\"**.\n\n4.  **Parallel Operation Blocks (Middle Row):**\n    *   These two blocks are aligned horizontally side-by-side.\n    *   **Left Block (Normalization Path):**\n        *   **Shape:** Rectangle with rounded corners, filled with solid teal.\n        *   **Content:** Contains a white icon of a bar chart or equalizer (vertical bars of varying heights) representing normalization. Text reads **\"Normalize\"** in white.\n        *   **Connection:** An arrow exits the bottom, curving inward toward the center line.\n    *   **Right Block (Rejection Path):**\n        *   **Shape:** Rectangle with rounded corners, filled with solid teal.\n        *   **Content:** Contains a white \"X\" mark or trash bin icon representing rejection. Text reads **\"Reject sample\"** in white.\n        *   **Connection:** An arrow exits the bottom, curving inward toward the center line.\n\n5.  **Operation Block 2 (Output - Conditional):**\n    *   *Note: Based on the flow \"Normalize → Output\", this block follows the \"Yes\" path.*\n    *   **Shape:** Rectangle with rounded corners, filled with solid teal. Positioned below the \"Normalize\" block but aligned centrally relative to the whole diagram.\n    *   **Content:** Contains a white icon of a tray with an arrow pointing out (export/output symbol). Text reads **\"Output\"** in white.\n    *   **Connection:** The arrow from \"Normalize\" leads here. An arrow exits the bottom, joining the main vertical flow.\n\n6.  **End Node:**\n    *   **Shape:** A pill-shaped rectangle (rounded ends), identical in width to the Start node.\n    *   **Content:** Filled with solid teal. Contains a white \"Stop\" square icon on the left and the text **\"End\"** in white, bold, sans-serif font.\n    *   **Connection:** Receives inputs from both the \"Output\" block (via the main central line) and the \"Reject sample\" block (via a connecting line merging from the right).\n\n**Typography:**\n*   Font family: Noto Sans or similar clean geometric sans-serif.\n*   Weight: Bold for headers/labels inside nodes.\n*   Size: Large enough to be legible (approx. 14-16pt relative to canvas).\n*   Alignment: Centered within nodes, or left-aligned next to icons.\n\n**Visual Consistency Notes:**\n*   Ensure all teal fills are uniform.\n*   Ensure all white icons are simple, flat vectors (no gradients or shadows).\n*   The \"Quality check\" diamond must clearly look like a decision point distinct from the process blocks.\n*   Arrows should have triangular heads and consistent thickness (approx. 2-3px).",
  "figureContract": {
    "version": "2026-10-10.v1",
    "id": "workflow",
    "path": "过程、时间与控制 / 流程图",
    "definition": "表达操作顺序、分支和终止条件",
